{"suggestions": [{"label": "ICT_TICT_CT", "reason": "The CT test now has a converged S0 geometry to run at, but the group reports only ground_state_geometry/ground_state_energy: no orbital character, charges or hole-electron separation exists yet. Gas phase, neutral singlet, one conformer of the ten embedded parents, aTB1, frequencies not computed (minimum unverified) - a starting point, not evidence either way.", "refs": ["execution:1707fd0a8fca07475cd4", "execution:1707fd0a8fca07475cd4:E001"]}, {"label": "RADIATIVE_RATE_STATE_BALANCE", "reason": "Bright/dark ordering and oscillator strengths remain entirely unmeasured; an S0 energy and geometry cannot inform the radiative/nonradiative balance, only enable the later vertical calculation.", "refs": ["execution:1707fd0a8fca07475cd4:E001"]}, {"label": "RIM_RIR_RIV", "reason": "Torsional coordinates (decyloxy tail, aryl-isocyanide, aryl-Au) are now fixed once, but no frequencies, barriers or rates were produced; convergence is a force criterion only and one conformer is not an ensemble, so torsion arguments still rest on the structural prior.", "refs": ["execution:1707fd0a8fca07475cd4", "execution:1707fd0a8fca07475cd4:E001"]}, {"label": "TRIPLET_METAL_ENERGY_TRANSFER", "reason": "No S/T ordering or SOC magnitudes at this geometry (estimate_soc_amesp remains disabled); the heavy-atom channel is still untested, so confidence should not move on this result.", "refs": ["execution:1707fd0a8fca07475cd4:E001"]}, {"label": "AGGREGATE_EXCITON_EXCIMER", "reason": "Single gas-phase monomer: no dimer, stacking or excimer model, so this result can neither support nor exclude aggregate emission and cannot represent C6F5 contacts.", "refs": ["execution:1707fd0a8fca07475cd4:E001"]}, {"label": "PACKING_HOST_MATRIX_CONFINEMENT", "reason": "Condensed-phase confinement needs packing/dimer data; a gas-phase monomer geometry leaves Q_RIM_VS_PACKING unresolved rather than favouring either side.", "refs": ["execution:1707fd0a8fca07475cd4", "execution:1707fd0a8fca07475cd4:E001"]}], "text": "New result group: one successful ground-state geometry recovery (amesp_aTB1, gas phase, ASE-BFGS in Cartesian coordinates, converged in 185 steps / 186 force evaluations, max atomic force 0.01941 eV/Å against a 0.02 target, final energy -89.89754 Ha, 56 atoms / 31 heavy, atom order preserved, charge 0 singlet, artifact geometry:b5d99bc4... produced and reusable). Execution details that matter: `minimum_verified_by_frequencies` = false; exactly one conformer was optimized (conformer 0 of ten embedded parents); no classical force field was available (MMFF94/UFF absent), so the geometry is semiempirical aTB1 rather than a force-field structure; no excited states, orbitals, spectrum or rates were produced.

This is a prerequisite checkpoint, not mechanism evidence: it supports no candidate's physics and refutes none. What changes is bookkeeping — the "no optimized S0 geometry" gap that gated the geometry-dependent questions is closed, while Q_CT_LOCAL and Q_TRIPLET_CHANNEL remain unanswered. Live limitations: an unverified minimum, a single conformer, and a gas-phase monomer are weakest exactly where the flexible decyloxy tail and the aryl–Au/aryl–isocyanide torsions matter, so no torsion, barrier or packing claim should cite this result; Q_RIM_VS_PACKING stays unresolved and a monomer cannot address condensed-phase confinement or aggregation. Method provenance should stay visible: later vertical/TD calculations at this geometry inherit an aTB1, one-conformer structure.

A useful next contrast is a vertical excited-state pass at this fixed geometry (state ordering, oscillator strengths, dominant transition character, S/T gaps and SOC) — that would separate bright CT vs dark S1 and the triplet channel, whereas a monomer torsion scan or a dimer comparison is what would actually touch RIM vs packing. HOST_GUEST_INTERACTION, ESIPT_PT and PET_ET are unchanged by this group (structural category mismatches persist)."}

